      "text": "Put the meat in a heavy pot with the wine, the garlic, the herbs, the salt and the pepper. Cover and cook in a very low oven until the meat falls apart and sits in a pool of clear fat. Take out the herbs, lift the meat from the fat and pull it into ragged threads with a pair of forks. Mix in enough of the warm fat to make it spreadable, add the nutmeg, and taste. Pack it firmly into jars and seal the tops with a layer of fat. Keep it cold.",
